# the master knobs: the starting assignments, the knob rows in GLO, the MASTER pot as a DJ filter, BPM
expectknob 0 0
expectknob 1 1
expectknob 2 3
expectknob 3 4
expectdj 0 64
# SELECT is the DJ filter (the middle is off), PRESETS is FX 1's amount, ALGORITHM is FX 2's
turn SELECT 5
expectdj 0 74
turn PRESET -5
expectfxamt 0 90
turn ALGO 4
expectfxamt 1 108
# GLO: the MASTER KNOB row is the eleventh (TEMPO, VOLUME, DJ, RESO, three rows for each FX, then the knobs); K2 changes what it does: VOLUME -> DJ FILTER
tap GLO
expect view 3
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K2 1
expectknob 0 1
shot knobs_glo.png
# the pot is the filter only once it has been moved
master 2048
wait 100
expectdj 0 74
master 3000
wait 100
expectdj 0 109
# the list has no OFF and no MACRO: from the last one, on goes round to VOLUME
turn K2 1
turn K2 1
turn K2 1
turn K2 1
expectknob 0 5
turn K2 1
expectknob 0 0
# BPM: on an encoder it is a whole BPM a detent; on the MASTER pot 0..127 spans 30 .. 300
turn K1 1
turn K2 1
turn K2 1
turn K2 1
turn K2 1
expectknob 1 5
turn SELECT 3
expect bpm 1280
turn SELECT -1
expect bpm 1270
shot knobs_bpm.png
